1
00:00:00,330 --> 00:00:02,240
[Previously]
If you're really set on leaving,

2
00:00:02,570 --> 00:00:04,090
I'll let you take the exam in Bangkok.

3
00:00:04,213 --> 00:00:06,360
And stop thinking I'm so mean.

4
00:00:06,576 --> 00:00:08,653
I love you more than
anyone in this family, dumbass.

5
00:00:08,677 --> 00:00:09,720
You can't leave me, okay?

6
00:00:11,414 --> 00:00:13,123
- Promise?
- Promise.

7
00:00:20,415 --> 00:00:21,416
Where is Tokyo?

8
00:00:29,384 --> 00:00:30,385
Blue!

9
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:43,201
Yi.

10
00:00:43,827 --> 00:00:45,000
Give me your sister's phone.

11
00:00:47,576 --> 00:00:48,577
From now on,

12
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:52,040
you're not allowed to contact anyone.

13
00:00:54,344 --> 00:00:55,800
Dad, you can't do this.

14
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:00,901
Tokyo.

15
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:08,801
Don't you feel guilty that your
mother died because of them?

16
00:01:10,096 --> 00:01:12,720
You told me Mom died in an accident.

17
00:01:13,856 --> 00:01:16,059
Dad, please. She's learned her lesson.

18
00:01:16,118 --> 00:01:17,360
And you, Yi.

19
00:01:17,845 --> 00:01:19,243
You're still taking her side?

20
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:25,360
If you don't break up with that girl,

21
00:01:27,254 --> 00:01:29,440
I'll chain you up at home

22
00:01:30,352 --> 00:01:31,829
and never let you
set foot outside again.

23
00:01:31,853 --> 00:01:33,500
Who I decide to date
is none of your business.

24
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:34,521
You're my daughter.

25
00:01:35,421 --> 00:01:36,960
You do what I tell you to do.

26
00:01:37,526 --> 00:01:38,527
Understand?

27
00:01:41,878 --> 00:01:42,960
That girl

28
00:01:44,264 --> 00:01:45,944
is the reason you've turned out like this.

29
00:01:46,283 --> 00:01:48,512
- See?
- Dad, can you stop acting crazy?

30
00:01:50,054 --> 00:01:52,280
Everything that's
happened is because of you.

31
00:01:52,624 --> 00:01:54,196
You're the one who picked
a fight with that family

32
00:01:54,220 --> 00:01:56,160
just because you didn't
get the port concession.

33
00:01:56,470 --> 00:01:58,950
If anyone has to die because
of this, it'll be because of you.

34
00:01:59,230 --> 00:02:00,240
Dad! Dad!

35
00:02:04,774 --> 00:02:06,320
I'm not breaking up with Blue.

36
00:02:08,352 --> 00:02:11,253
We have nothing to
do with your stupid feud.

37
00:02:11,263 --> 00:02:12,560
- Tokyo!
- Dad!

38
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:14,801
Dad!

39
00:02:16,440 --> 00:02:19,120
Dad, just let her go. She doesn't
know anything. She's still a kid.

40
00:02:20,141 --> 00:02:21,142
Please, Dad.

41
00:02:23,819 --> 00:02:25,120
She's still a kid?

42
00:02:28,918 --> 00:02:30,400
Fine, if you said she's still a kid.

43
00:02:33,523 --> 00:02:35,430
Yi! Dad!

44
00:02:38,702 --> 00:02:39,703
Dad!

45
00:02:42,102 --> 00:02:44,103
Since your brother knew
about it and kept quiet,

46
00:02:44,848 --> 00:02:46,304
he'll take the punishment for you.

47
00:02:48,715 --> 00:02:50,216
Dad! No!

48
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:53,120
Dad!

49
00:02:57,500 --> 00:03:01,500
"Juliet &amp; Juliet"
(Episode 6)

50
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:11,400
Give me your phone.

51
00:03:13,174 --> 00:03:14,175
No.

52
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,176
You have no right to take it.

53
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:19,170
It's mine.

54
00:03:21,750 --> 00:03:24,160
As long as you're still
living off this family,

55
00:03:25,170 --> 00:03:26,720
you have to obey your parents.

56
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:31,641
Mom!

57
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:36,501
I just have a girlfriend.

58
00:03:37,601 --> 00:03:39,232
I haven't done anything wrong.

59
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:42,240
- What is wrong with you and Dad?
- Of course you've done something wrong.

60
00:03:44,902 --> 00:03:46,303
You still don't get it, do you?

61
00:03:47,141 --> 00:03:49,100
This isn't just about you anymore.

62
00:03:52,246 --> 00:03:54,947
You're causing trouble for everyone.

63
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:06,141
I never raised you to be like this.

64
00:04:09,251 --> 00:04:12,252
You're selfish. You only
think about yourself.

65
00:04:15,808 --> 00:04:18,509
Have you ever thought about
anyone else involved in this?

66
00:04:39,576 --> 00:04:41,300
This is a matter of life and death.

67
00:04:43,267 --> 00:04:46,150
It's not just about two people
being in love like you think.

68
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:11,180
Forget about Tokyo.

69
00:05:14,862 --> 00:05:16,200
You don't get a choice.

70
00:05:26,920 --> 00:05:29,080
I've already arranged for
you to move out of the dorm.

71
00:05:30,840 --> 00:05:31,841
From now on,

72
00:05:33,041 --> 00:05:34,654
you're moving back home.

73
00:07:28,913 --> 00:07:29,914
Dad.

74
00:07:32,070 --> 00:07:34,630
What are you going to ask for
on your sister's behalf this time?

75
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,001
Dad.

76
00:07:39,300 --> 00:07:41,439
She just wants to go to school in Bangkok.

77
00:07:44,584 --> 00:07:46,300
Can't we just let her go?

78
00:07:46,885 --> 00:07:48,485
Let her transfer to a school in Bangkok.

79
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,001
Let her try being with
that girl for a while.

80
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:52,700
They'll break up eventually, Dad.

81
00:07:53,901 --> 00:07:55,802
It's just teenage love.

82
00:07:56,035 --> 00:07:57,360
We don't need to interfere.

83
00:07:59,036 --> 00:08:00,037
Love?

84
00:08:02,166 --> 00:08:03,200
Don't you remember

85
00:08:05,046 --> 00:08:07,447
someone once used love as an excuse

86
00:08:08,547 --> 00:08:10,960
and left us to pay the price for it?

87
00:08:13,651 --> 00:08:14,880
If you don't remember,

88
00:08:15,928 --> 00:08:16,960
I'll remind you

89
00:08:19,624 --> 00:08:22,350
who started all of this in the first place.

90
00:08:29,123 --> 00:08:30,551
But you're right about one thing.

91
00:08:33,854 --> 00:08:34,855
Your sister

92
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,440
shouldn't have to be
involved in this vendetta.

93
00:08:57,724 --> 00:08:59,800
Keep a close eye on her.

94
00:09:03,115 --> 00:09:05,130
Don't let her stray again.

95
00:09:06,700 --> 00:09:07,701
Understand?

96
00:09:26,731 --> 00:09:27,732
Tokyo.

97
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:30,875
I've asked Jai and Pupay
to pick you up outside the school.

98
00:09:31,942 --> 00:09:33,200
Stay close to those two.

99
00:09:46,691 --> 00:09:47,692
Hi.

100
00:10:00,270 --> 00:10:02,900
Hey, there's a new TikTok
challenge. Let's do it.

101
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:24,501
Sorry.

102
00:11:00,336 --> 00:11:01,360
Phakjira.

103
00:11:01,750 --> 00:11:04,751
It seems you've been causing more trouble
than you realize lately.

104
00:11:08,032 --> 00:11:09,933
I want you to stay out of trouble.

105
00:11:11,033 --> 00:11:14,643
You'd better stay away from
anyone you shouldn't be involved with.

106
00:11:16,045 --> 00:11:17,360
And one more thing.

107
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:20,960
If you disobey me, you might
not graduate with your classmates.

108
00:11:23,363 --> 00:11:25,440
And that dream you've been chasing

109
00:11:27,038 --> 00:11:28,640
will remain nothing but a dream.

110
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:30,901
Understand?

111
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:35,568
Hello? What's up, Dad?

112
00:12:36,528 --> 00:12:37,529
I'm at school.

113
00:12:41,494 --> 00:12:42,865
Where the hell are you looking?

114
00:12:46,323 --> 00:12:49,600
Don't you think Pupay's
been acting weird lately?

115
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:53,001
Weird how?

116
00:12:56,595 --> 00:12:59,720
I don't know. She's
been acting kind of shady.

117
00:13:01,950 --> 00:13:05,240
You think she's been
telling her family about you?

118
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:15,536
Okay, Tokyo, seriously.

119
00:13:16,080 --> 00:13:18,712
Since when does Pupay ever stick
her nose into other people's business?

120
00:13:18,736 --> 00:13:21,800
I can gossip with the
girl next door for an hour,

121
00:13:21,984 --> 00:13:24,144
and she just sits there
listening without even caring.

122
00:13:24,440 --> 00:13:26,160
Why would she go tell her family about you?

123
00:13:27,408 --> 00:13:30,360
Yeah, maybe I'm overthinking it.

124
00:13:30,976 --> 00:13:32,360
But think about it.

125
00:13:33,056 --> 00:13:35,840
Her family's having money problems,
and her dad owes my family money.

126
00:13:36,032 --> 00:13:38,312
Then all of a sudden,
she shows up with a brand-new phone.

127
00:13:38,464 --> 00:13:40,024
How am I supposed
to not be suspicious?

128
00:13:41,872 --> 00:13:44,880
Okay, seriously.

129
00:13:45,499 --> 00:13:48,400
Is there anyone besides your family
who doesn't owe your family money?

130
00:13:48,920 --> 00:13:50,280
Even I do.

131
00:13:51,176 --> 00:13:53,400
So are you suspicious of me too?

132
00:13:57,699 --> 00:13:59,272
Exactly.

133
00:14:00,340 --> 00:14:01,341
See?

134
00:14:02,160 --> 00:14:03,750
Then couldn't it be anyone?

135
00:14:05,761 --> 00:14:07,841
- I don't know.
- You really want to know, don't you?

136
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:10,201
Here. Check it.

137
00:14:10,800 --> 00:14:13,450
Then you'll know whether I'm the one
who went running to your dad.

138
00:14:16,600 --> 00:14:18,440
- Pupay.
- Hey, you want to check my cloud too?

139
00:14:18,744 --> 00:14:19,960
Go ahead and check that too.

140
00:14:20,414 --> 00:14:22,574
Then maybe you'll finally stop wondering
if it was me.

141
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:25,282
It's not what you think...

142
00:14:25,307 --> 00:14:27,307
If you really saw me as
your friend from the start,

143
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:29,600
why would you suspect
me in the first place?

144
00:14:33,822 --> 00:14:35,760
- Pupay!
- Pupay!

145
00:14:35,806 --> 00:14:36,807
Pupay, wait.

146
00:14:38,100 --> 00:14:39,101
Pupay!

147
00:14:39,347 --> 00:14:41,820
- Pupay, wait!
- Wait for Tokyo.

148
00:14:44,611 --> 00:14:45,612
Hey.

149
00:14:46,019 --> 00:14:48,120
- I'm sorry.
- What's the point of apologizing now?

150
00:14:50,702 --> 00:14:53,462
Deep down, you think I'm just like
all your other friends, don't you?

151
00:14:54,990 --> 00:14:56,191
You think I'm only friends with you
because of your money,

152
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:58,520
because of your family,
because of who your dad is, right?

153
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:00,800
Well, let me tell you something.

154
00:15:01,091 --> 00:15:03,300
I've never even cared
who the hell your dad is.

155
00:15:05,408 --> 00:15:07,160
I just like being with you.
I like hanging out with you guys.

156
00:15:07,180 --> 00:15:08,900
Because you never cared that I was poor,

157
00:15:08,960 --> 00:15:10,560
unlike what everyone else says about me.

158
00:15:13,126 --> 00:15:14,720
But if being friends with
me makes you uncomfortable

159
00:15:14,740 --> 00:15:16,860
or you don't feel okay being
friends with me anymore,

160
00:15:17,280 --> 00:15:19,240
then we just don't have
to be friends. That's it.

161
00:15:29,115 --> 00:15:31,531
It's okay. She's probably still mad.

162
00:15:31,622 --> 00:15:32,942
Just give her some space for now.

163
00:15:33,371 --> 00:15:36,160
You can talk to her once she's calmed down.

164
00:15:46,323 --> 00:15:47,500
You two.

165
00:15:49,278 --> 00:15:50,279
Come here.

166
00:15:57,750 --> 00:15:59,640
From now on, you're both blacklisted.

167
00:16:00,408 --> 00:16:02,520
You're not allowed to
meet in the library anymore.

168
00:16:05,409 --> 00:16:06,410
Get out.

169
00:16:25,062 --> 00:16:27,860
Tokyo, Miss Vee wants
to see you in her office.

170
00:16:28,211 --> 00:16:30,491
She said you haven't turned
in all your club assignments.

171
00:16:32,390 --> 00:16:33,391
The club?

172
00:16:34,016 --> 00:16:35,017
What club?

173
00:16:37,280 --> 00:16:38,640
She called Blue in too.

174
00:16:39,281 --> 00:16:41,641
I think she wants to talk about
you moving out of the dorm.

175
00:16:46,896 --> 00:16:50,160
You haven't turned in all your
Environmental Club reports, Tokyo.

176
00:16:52,163 --> 00:16:53,600
Environmental Club?

177
00:16:55,827 --> 00:16:58,828
No, I'm in the Literature Club.

178
00:17:01,320 --> 00:17:02,440
Oh, really?

179
00:17:04,921 --> 00:17:06,722
Then your name must've
been added by mistake.

180
00:17:06,922 --> 00:17:09,800
But that's okay. Write the
report now and hand it in to me

181
00:17:09,891 --> 00:17:10,892
so you can pass.

182
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:14,500
And you, Phakjira.

183
00:17:14,718 --> 00:17:16,576
Even though you've already
moved out of the dorm,

184
00:17:16,600 --> 00:17:18,601
you left your room in a terrible mess.

185
00:17:19,300 --> 00:17:21,601
So sit right next to her
and write an apology letter.

186
00:17:23,400 --> 00:17:24,401
Okay.

187
00:17:25,510 --> 00:17:28,443
You two stay here and finish your work.

188
00:17:29,024 --> 00:17:30,025
I'll be back.

189
00:18:00,350 --> 00:18:01,351
How are you doing?

190
00:18:02,819 --> 00:18:04,700
I'm okay. What about you?

191
00:18:05,374 --> 00:18:07,201
Yeah, I'm fine.

192
00:18:10,792 --> 00:18:14,793
I think Miss Vee might be
the only teacher in this school

193
00:18:15,400 --> 00:18:16,501
who's actually on our side.

194
00:18:26,392 --> 00:18:27,393
But yesterday,

195
00:18:28,750 --> 00:18:30,320
my dad was furious.

196
00:18:32,371 --> 00:18:35,560
He brought up my mom's death

197
00:18:37,326 --> 00:18:40,440
and said it had something to do
with the Monchaitrakul family.

198
00:18:45,678 --> 00:18:47,920
Do you know anything about that?

199
00:18:55,171 --> 00:18:56,571
I've never heard anything about it.

200
00:19:00,880 --> 00:19:03,881
I thought Uncle Wirat's death

201
00:19:04,200 --> 00:19:06,201
was what started this whole stupid feud.

202
00:19:07,795 --> 00:19:09,120
So your mom was involved too?

203
00:19:12,147 --> 00:19:15,880
I think my dad's always tried to avoid
talking about my mom.

204
00:19:17,248 --> 00:19:20,760
But he was so angry last
night that he let it slip.

205
00:19:23,739 --> 00:19:27,000
I think if we want to
put an end to all this,

206
00:19:27,740 --> 00:19:29,701
we might have to find the answers together

207
00:19:31,041 --> 00:19:32,401
and figure out how it all started.

208
00:19:34,107 --> 00:19:35,108
Yeah.

209
00:20:44,320 --> 00:20:45,321
Anything?

210
00:20:55,094 --> 00:20:56,095
Here.

211
00:20:56,896 --> 00:20:58,680
Here it is. The article about my mom.

212
00:20:58,700 --> 00:21:00,203
[Woman Killed in Car Fire,
Child Miraculously Survives]

213
00:21:00,227 --> 00:21:03,110
My dad and brothers
always told me

214
00:21:03,134 --> 00:21:05,200
that my mom died in a car fire.

215
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:13,480
This one must be about Pakkard's dad.

216
00:21:13,920 --> 00:21:16,280
Businessman Named Wirat
Brutally Killed in Robbery.

217
00:21:16,458 --> 00:21:18,738
Why does everything keep happening in cars?
Look at this.

218
00:21:19,573 --> 00:21:21,379
[Kongpurim Secures Port
Concession for Decades]

219
00:21:21,403 --> 00:21:23,046
It's just like my dad told me.

220
00:21:24,550 --> 00:21:25,960
As soon as Uncle Wirat died,

221
00:21:28,342 --> 00:21:30,243
Kongpurim got the concession.

222
00:21:46,694 --> 00:21:48,300
It can't be a coincidence

223
00:21:49,915 --> 00:21:51,635
that all these events are connected, right?

224
00:21:54,680 --> 00:21:55,681
No.

225
00:21:57,416 --> 00:21:59,217
But if we ask anyone about this,

226
00:22:00,920 --> 00:22:02,621
I doubt they'll tell us the truth.

227
00:22:14,264 --> 00:22:15,265
But there's one person

228
00:22:16,878 --> 00:22:18,040
who can't lie to us.

229
00:22:39,470 --> 00:22:40,471
Amen.

230
00:22:48,518 --> 00:22:50,398
Father, there's something
we'd like to ask you.

231
00:22:51,632 --> 00:22:53,100
We'd like you to answer us, Father.

232
00:22:55,056 --> 00:22:56,440
If I can answer, I will.

233
00:23:05,918 --> 00:23:07,420
Seventeen years ago,

234
00:23:10,056 --> 00:23:11,720
what happened to my mother?

235
00:23:16,184 --> 00:23:17,600
Please don't lie to us, Father.

236
00:23:20,526 --> 00:23:21,760
God is listening.

237
00:23:25,368 --> 00:23:26,800
Did my mother's death

238
00:23:28,206 --> 00:23:29,960
have something to do with Mr. Wirat?

239
00:23:32,439 --> 00:23:34,955
Yes. But I can't tell you everything.

240
00:23:35,088 --> 00:23:36,089
I wasn't there.

241
00:23:36,795 --> 00:23:40,683
But what I can tell you is that
the feud between the two families

242
00:23:41,190 --> 00:23:42,191
started with Wirat

243
00:23:45,200 --> 00:23:47,400
and Sirin, your mother.

244
00:24:00,043 --> 00:24:01,760
But there's no way my mother

245
00:24:02,070 --> 00:24:04,875
would've held a grudge against anyone
or hurt anyone, right?

246
00:24:05,494 --> 00:24:07,876
It wasn't hatred that started it all.

247
00:24:25,307 --> 00:24:26,308
Tokyo.

248
00:24:28,128 --> 00:24:29,129
It's time to go home.

249
00:24:33,129 --> 00:24:35,850
You should take your friend home too.

250
00:24:36,130 --> 00:24:37,300
Before anyone sees you.

251
00:24:46,622 --> 00:24:47,623
Go.

252
00:24:57,270 --> 00:24:58,640
I don't think it's broken.

253
00:24:59,568 --> 00:25:02,800
Oh, really? I wasn't sure.

254
00:25:02,982 --> 00:25:03,983
I saw it flickering.

255
00:25:04,640 --> 00:25:05,920
The bulb might be going out.

256
00:25:15,672 --> 00:25:17,800
How long have you worked here, Uncle Phu.

257
00:25:18,926 --> 00:25:20,080
Since before Blue was born.

258
00:25:20,606 --> 00:25:23,368
Wow, so

259
00:25:23,720 --> 00:25:26,200
you were already here
when Uncle Wirat was still alive, right?

260
00:25:27,136 --> 00:25:28,137
Yes, I was.

261
00:25:35,552 --> 00:25:36,553
So...

262
00:25:38,427 --> 00:25:40,000
how did Uncle Wirat die?

263
00:25:45,178 --> 00:25:46,378
You're better off not knowing.

264
00:25:47,579 --> 00:25:50,280
Please, Uncle Phu. I really need to know.

265
00:25:50,816 --> 00:25:52,817
No one in this family
will tell me anything.

266
00:25:53,736 --> 00:25:55,760
But I trust that you won't keep it from me.

267
00:26:01,680 --> 00:26:02,681
Back then,

268
00:26:04,254 --> 00:26:05,960
there was a lot of chaos in town.

269
00:26:06,912 --> 00:26:09,192
It was all because of the
fight over the port concession.

270
00:26:09,800 --> 00:26:10,801
That family

271
00:26:11,424 --> 00:26:13,300
made the first move and killed Mr. Wirat.

272
00:26:15,125 --> 00:26:16,520
They shot him dead

273
00:26:17,896 --> 00:26:20,940
and staged it as a robbery
to cover their tracks.

274
00:26:23,320 --> 00:26:24,360
They dared to do it

275
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:27,977
because Monchaitrakul was about to
win the province's biggest port concession.

276
00:26:28,001 --> 00:26:29,302
[Kongpurim Secures Port
Concession for Decades]

277
00:26:29,320 --> 00:26:30,960
No one dared go up against that family.

278
00:26:32,723 --> 00:26:35,243
That's why your father's held
onto this grudge all these years.

279
00:26:42,758 --> 00:26:44,300
Try to understand your father, Blue.

280
00:26:45,440 --> 00:26:46,480
If it were you,

281
00:26:46,694 --> 00:26:49,454
and your brother had been murdered,
you'd be angry too, wouldn't you?

282
00:27:04,326 --> 00:27:05,767
You two...

283
00:27:06,248 --> 00:27:07,249
I'm begging you.

284
00:27:08,168 --> 00:27:09,900
Can't you just be kids?

285
00:27:11,347 --> 00:27:13,245
Stay out of the adults' feud.

286
00:27:28,576 --> 00:27:29,577
You OK?

287
00:27:30,600 --> 00:27:33,720
Hey, I'm fine.

288
00:27:35,301 --> 00:27:36,781
I don't want to dwell on this either.

289
00:27:38,939 --> 00:27:39,960
The past is the past.

290
00:28:32,933 --> 00:28:34,800
- What's this?
- Money.

291
00:28:35,046 --> 00:28:36,166
Did your brain stop working?

292
00:28:37,880 --> 00:28:38,881
I know what it is.

293
00:28:41,300 --> 00:28:42,500
Where did you get it?

294
00:28:44,500 --> 00:28:47,400
It's mine. My savings.

295
00:28:49,000 --> 00:28:52,160
I think you and your girlfriend should
get out of this town as soon as you can.

296
00:28:53,846 --> 00:28:56,806
I have a feeling our family and theirs
are going to clash sooner or later.

297
00:28:59,371 --> 00:29:02,051
And I don't want you getting caught up
in this because of me again.

298
00:29:02,918 --> 00:29:06,200
It's not because of you.
It's because of Dad.

299
00:29:07,376 --> 00:29:08,377
It is because of me.

300
00:29:09,477 --> 00:29:11,637
Just tell me when you
and your girlfriend are leaving.

301
00:29:11,974 --> 00:29:14,000
The sooner, the better. Got it?

302
00:29:18,705 --> 00:29:21,840
But if Dad finds out, he'll kill you, Yi.

303
00:29:22,590 --> 00:29:24,230
Look at what he did to you the other day.

304
00:29:24,880 --> 00:29:26,280
That's probably the worst he'll do.

305
00:29:26,680 --> 00:29:28,000
At most, I'll be covered in poop.

306
00:29:28,201 --> 00:29:30,280
I've still got the eldest-son card to play.

307
00:29:30,800 --> 00:29:32,050
Dad won't let me die.

308
00:29:32,900 --> 00:29:35,000
I still have to carry on
the Kongpurim family line.

309
00:29:36,411 --> 00:29:37,520
Besides, I think

310
00:29:39,392 --> 00:29:41,020
this scar actually looks pretty cool.

311
00:29:41,393 --> 00:29:42,394
Right?

312
00:29:45,024 --> 00:29:46,425
Ow! Ow!

313
00:29:46,896 --> 00:29:48,400
That hurts! What are you doing?

314
00:29:49,035 --> 00:29:50,600
Who told you to joke about that?

315
00:29:53,835 --> 00:29:55,130
Come here. Give me a hug.

316
00:29:58,732 --> 00:30:00,840
- You smell like poop.
- Ew, snot!

317
00:30:01,739 --> 00:30:03,019
I don't want to hug you anymore.

318
00:30:03,635 --> 00:30:04,636
Gross.

319
00:30:31,102 --> 00:30:32,103
Please help me out, sir.

320
00:30:32,920 --> 00:30:34,440
Whatever you want,

321
00:30:34,859 --> 00:30:36,520
I'll make it worth your while.

322
00:30:42,456 --> 00:30:43,656
All right, I'll call you back.

323
00:30:45,560 --> 00:30:48,240
Boss, I managed to recover
the corrupted CCTV footage.

324
00:31:05,046 --> 00:31:07,966
- [Everything's going according to plan.]
- Should we wait for the police?

325
00:31:11,900 --> 00:31:14,608
[Temporarily Closed for Renovation
Do Not Enter Without Permission]

326
00:31:14,633 --> 00:31:16,360
Go all out.

327
00:31:18,400 --> 00:31:19,960
Come on, give it everything you've got!

328
00:31:34,600 --> 00:31:35,701
Is something wrong, Boss?

329
00:31:42,800 --> 00:31:44,920
Your daughter needs
regular dialysis, doesn't she?

330
00:31:46,600 --> 00:31:47,920
How much does it cost a month?

331
00:31:50,939 --> 00:31:52,440
I'm not like the Kongpurims.

332
00:31:53,040 --> 00:31:55,200
I don't go around killing people.

333
00:31:56,240 --> 00:31:57,241
I'm a businessman.

334
00:31:57,800 --> 00:32:00,840
Businessmen negotiate with money.

335
00:32:03,525 --> 00:32:05,760
I'll pay off all her hospital bills,

336
00:32:06,785 --> 00:32:08,900
and I'll pay for your
daughter's education too.

337
00:32:10,560 --> 00:32:13,320
All you have to do is testify
against the Kongpurims.

338
00:32:14,376 --> 00:32:15,377
Deal?

339
00:32:34,331 --> 00:32:35,750
Mr. Wiboon, are you sure

340
00:32:36,352 --> 00:32:38,472
you have evidence that the
Kongpurims were behind it?

341
00:32:43,051 --> 00:32:44,052
I'm sure.

342
00:32:45,067 --> 00:32:46,480
Inspector, please give me a moment.

343
00:32:47,200 --> 00:32:48,600
My witness is on his way.

344
00:33:02,038 --> 00:33:04,000
Boss, the witness has been assassinated.

345
00:33:12,700 --> 00:33:15,201
[Chanthabun Provincial Police Station]

346
00:33:21,900 --> 00:33:23,260
Don't do anything.

347
00:33:24,300 --> 00:33:25,720
Our time is almost here.

348
00:33:47,080 --> 00:33:48,280
Why are you giving this to me?

349
00:33:50,646 --> 00:33:53,558
Well, I don't know who else to give it to.

350
00:33:56,166 --> 00:33:57,686
I probably won't be taking it with me.

351
00:34:00,880 --> 00:34:02,440
So you're really going through with it?

352
00:34:03,931 --> 00:34:06,251
I thought you were just making up
some crazy plan for fun.

353
00:34:08,875 --> 00:34:09,876
I'm not joking.

354
00:34:10,837 --> 00:34:11,838
I'm serious.

355
00:34:14,696 --> 00:34:17,100
We probably can't meet
at the library anymore.

356
00:34:17,841 --> 00:34:18,842
So...

357
00:34:19,759 --> 00:34:20,999
how about we meet here instead?

358
00:34:22,938 --> 00:34:25,098
Tokyo and I have been
thinking about this for a while.

359
00:34:27,500 --> 00:34:30,639
We're going to run away together.

360
00:34:32,928 --> 00:34:34,929
We won't have to keep hiding anymore.

361
00:34:35,600 --> 00:34:37,700
We'll leave as soon as
our final exams are over.

362
00:34:38,190 --> 00:34:40,960
And Yi really knows about this, right?

363
00:34:42,900 --> 00:34:43,901
Yeah.

364
00:34:45,112 --> 00:34:46,700
He already promised Tokyo he'd help us.

365
00:34:49,645 --> 00:34:51,005
I put a prepaid SIM in it for you.

366
00:34:52,851 --> 00:34:53,852
Thank you.

367
00:34:56,649 --> 00:34:59,392
Yi, it's tomorrow.

368
00:35:11,950 --> 00:35:14,700
You've got me. What are you scared of?

369
00:35:19,592 --> 00:35:21,400
And answer your phone when I call, okay?

370
00:35:22,046 --> 00:35:24,486
Don't run away from home
and start acting like some wild kid.

371
00:35:26,125 --> 00:35:28,520
I'll answer. I know.

372
00:35:33,672 --> 00:35:34,880
After this,

373
00:35:35,774 --> 00:35:37,814
we probably won't get to
see each other very often.

374
00:35:48,048 --> 00:35:49,049
Yeah.

375
00:35:50,800 --> 00:35:52,120
I will send you off, don't worry.

376
00:35:56,763 --> 00:35:58,464
Thanks.

377
00:36:03,867 --> 00:36:05,160
You're gonna miss me, right?

378
00:36:07,739 --> 00:36:08,840
Of course I am.

379
00:36:14,102 --> 00:36:15,582
Are you sure you can handle yourself?

380
00:36:21,205 --> 00:36:22,206
I'll be fine.

381
00:37:16,200 --> 00:37:17,201
Jai.

382
00:37:18,401 --> 00:37:20,440
Just stop running away.

383
00:37:20,549 --> 00:37:23,344
You know you can never
escape the Kongpurims.

384
00:37:25,536 --> 00:37:26,537
What about you?

385
00:37:30,435 --> 00:37:32,140
Have you been spying on me for my family?

386
00:37:34,040 --> 00:37:35,441
Can you not say that?

387
00:37:36,241 --> 00:37:40,040
You know how much my
life depends on your family.

388
00:37:40,771 --> 00:37:43,472
My family still owes your dad money.

389
00:37:44,835 --> 00:37:47,048
And then there's the school singer thing.

390
00:37:47,363 --> 00:37:48,976
If the teachers weren't trying
to stay on your good side,

391
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:50,800
do you think I'd even
get to perform onstage?

392
00:37:52,419 --> 00:37:55,480
If I don't become a
singer, if I don't make it big,

393
00:37:55,720 --> 00:37:57,120
how am I ever gonna be rich like you?

394
00:37:57,140 --> 00:37:58,880
Can you just stop talking?

395
00:38:01,214 --> 00:38:03,840
Fine. I'll stop.

396
00:38:05,843 --> 00:38:08,360
But if I do, will you come home with me?

397
00:38:20,600 --> 00:38:22,240
This guy grabbed my boobs!

398
00:38:22,260 --> 00:38:24,700
Hey, hey! Watch what you're saying.
I didn't do anything!

399
00:38:51,600 --> 00:38:52,601
Are you okay?

400
00:39:00,766 --> 00:39:02,160
Jai betrayed us.

401
00:39:05,700 --> 00:39:07,220
She's been spying on us for my family.

402
00:39:13,800 --> 00:39:15,040
It's okay.

403
00:39:16,254 --> 00:39:17,960
Maybe your dad forced her to do it.

404
00:39:23,603 --> 00:39:24,604
No.

405
00:39:27,300 --> 00:39:28,600
She chose to do it herself.

406
00:39:44,459 --> 00:39:45,560
I don't even know anymore

407
00:39:46,624 --> 00:39:48,600
if she ever really wanted

408
00:39:51,542 --> 00:39:53,440
to be my friend all this time.

409
00:40:06,315 --> 00:40:08,435
There's no point trying to
figure that out right now.

410
00:40:10,316 --> 00:40:14,040
Once we get out of here,
we can find the answer together, okay?

411
00:40:22,700 --> 00:40:24,200
But I don't know

412
00:40:25,662 --> 00:40:29,300
if I'll ever want to believe
anything she says again.

413
00:40:40,224 --> 00:40:41,500
It's almost nine.

414
00:40:45,816 --> 00:40:47,300
Yi should be here soon.

415
00:41:09,900 --> 00:41:11,600
[Pakkard: Those two changed the plan.]

416
00:41:11,710 --> 00:41:13,670
[Meet under the railway
bridge at the same time.]

417
00:41:29,957 --> 00:41:32,360
I can't even tell what's tears
and what's rain anymore.

418
00:41:48,104 --> 00:41:49,800
But Yi's really coming, right?

419
00:41:58,000 --> 00:41:59,700
Yi would never break his promise to us.

420
00:42:11,432 --> 00:42:12,433
Where are those two?

421
00:42:21,608 --> 00:42:22,609
Huh?

422
00:42:26,176 --> 00:42:27,400
How did my dad die?

423
00:42:48,368 --> 00:42:49,369
Hello, Yi?

424
00:42:52,165 --> 00:42:53,280
Where's my sister?

425
00:42:54,400 --> 00:42:57,001
What the hell, Pakkard?
What's wrong with you?

426
00:42:57,500 --> 00:42:59,450
Tell me how my dad died.

427
00:43:01,120 --> 00:43:02,121
What about Dad?

428
00:43:15,000 --> 00:43:16,001
Hurry, get inside.

429
00:43:17,419 --> 00:43:19,300
- What about you?
- We'll figure that out later.

430
00:43:21,700 --> 00:43:22,701
Go!

431
00:44:30,718 --> 00:44:32,130
Why the hell are you doing this?

432
00:44:37,846 --> 00:44:39,120
How did my dad die?

433
00:44:42,294 --> 00:44:43,974
What? What the hell are you talking about?

434
00:44:47,600 --> 00:44:48,601
Where's my sister?

435
00:44:49,900 --> 00:44:52,320
What the hell is wrong with you, Pakkard?

436
00:44:52,800 --> 00:44:54,640
Tell me how my dad died.

437
00:44:54,801 --> 00:44:56,900
You're the one who
killed my dad, aren't you?

438
00:44:59,000 --> 00:45:01,760
[Businessman named Wirat Brutally
Killed in Robbery Inside Luxury Car]

439
00:45:05,171 --> 00:45:06,362
Are you gonna tell me now?

440
00:45:13,000 --> 00:45:14,001
Pakkard.

441
00:45:15,300 --> 00:45:16,301
Calm down.

442
00:45:17,288 --> 00:45:18,880
Just calm down and listen to me.

443
00:45:20,043 --> 00:45:21,700
I don't know what you heard,

444
00:45:24,315 --> 00:45:25,555
but whatever you heard isn't true.

445
00:45:25,579 --> 00:45:27,379
Your family's the one
who's been lying to me.

446
00:45:27,659 --> 00:45:30,360
All of you are the reason
my life turned out like this.

447
00:45:30,526 --> 00:45:32,360
No, no. Calm down.

448
00:45:32,527 --> 00:45:33,528
Put the gun down.

449
00:45:34,280 --> 00:45:35,281
Just calm down.

450
00:45:36,120 --> 00:45:37,506
What the fuck? Are
you really gonna kill me?

451
00:45:37,530 --> 00:45:38,960
Go blame your father.

452
00:45:38,990 --> 00:45:42,070
I'm telling you, the reason your life
turned out like this is because of him.

453
00:46:29,648 --> 00:46:31,000
Why are you doing this?

454
00:47:01,384 --> 00:47:03,800
[Next Episode] Our family is
looking for Pakkard right now.

455
00:47:04,011 --> 00:47:06,930
My parents have taken
Pakkard to the border.

456
00:47:07,640 --> 00:47:09,500
So you helped Pakkard escape too?

457
00:47:10,041 --> 00:47:12,920
Do you still believe in
your pure, innocent love?

458
00:47:13,242 --> 00:47:14,720
Or do you think your love

459
00:47:15,056 --> 00:47:17,720
can wash away your
mother's blood from the past?

460
00:47:19,360 --> 00:47:21,760
Everything has already been decided.

461
00:47:21,904 --> 00:47:23,880
You just have to play your part.
